62 #uuid "1635a868-152f-5d33-a98e-b081e4cab5fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111541 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111542 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111542 #edb/ref 1061 193876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111542 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ae5c4a50-4790-50a4-8623-989e8ec2863b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111542 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111543 #edb/ref 1061 193879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111543 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fbb2518f-7e11-56ac-abf6-3669b2e06083" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111543 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111922 #edb/ref 1064 "Two angles are **supplementary** if their measures add up to $180^\\circ.$\n\n![](images/88/886f1ce19ad595b470d5ad13943b780bd5a22ee737908d9554e97bd08c9ce985.png)\n\nThese angles are supplementary because the sum of their measures is $180^\\circ{:}$\n\n$$\n105^\\circ +75^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nA **linear pair** is a pair of adjacent angles formed when two lines intersect. The angles shown above form a linear pair.\n\nThe **linear pair postulate** states the following:\n\nIf two angles form a linear pair, then they are supplementary.\n\nThe converse is *not* true. That is, if two angles are supplementary, they do not necessarily form a linear pair.\n\nTo see why, consider the diagram shown below:\n\n![](images/29/29ff0dfefb0b535342f4e8060b37fb2404983fc150681bb02d18fa6e5b00f899.png)\n\nAlthough the angles are supplementary (the sum of their measures is $120^\\circ + 60^\\circ = 180^\\circ$), they do not form a linear pair of angles since they are not adjacent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111922 #edb/ref 1065 9518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111922 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ea9626ef-f56f-5668-8f47-81a9f68c9db4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111922 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502984 #edb/ref