#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503670 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the measure of an angle that's supplementary to an angle of $(2x+65)^{∘}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503670 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "29678fcd-bdef-5e0e-a077-5ea622166f37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503670 #edb/ref 1074 "Two angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, the measure of an angle that's supplementary to an angle of $(2x+65)^{∘}$ must be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}-(2x+65)^{∘} & =(180-2x-65)^{∘} \\\\  & =(180-65-2x)^{∘} \\\\  & =(115-2x)^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503697 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503697 #edb/ref 1069 "q-237400" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503697 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503697 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/79/795f457314076b565d76a6b2579f2e1f87a247053dd0bb5de72225d63e17bf7f.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, what is the measure of $∠COD?$\n\n$m∠COD=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503697 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6af619db-0f0f-58ae-bb63-22eb9d582800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503697 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/70/7045c84435a9ed2934569aceabf9d01e01d4278de6b89329664b654dc53b5250.png)\n\nTwo angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘},$ a straight angle.\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, we have that $∠COD$ and $∠DOE$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm∠COD+m∠DOE={180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $∠COD$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠COD & ={180}^{∘}-m∠DOE \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{144}^{∘} \\\\  & ={36}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503702 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503702 #edb/ref 1069 "q-237318" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503702 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503702 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/63/633e75b1b02b1eba8f512af09a8