f an angle forming a linear pair with an angle of ${27}^{∘}$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}-{27}^{∘} & ={153}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503754 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503754 #edb/ref 1069 "q-237185" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503754 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503754 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/78/78d588198d35e69ca7ae2b199dd52d2c07e5c9d3268214821b737deffe5cb03d.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, what is the measure of $∠BOE?$\n\n$m∠BOE=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503754 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0518b35-857c-5bdb-a223-e7f6be6165f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503754 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/d3/d3ba77dd51c7d26685246304088d484144f5dcda57c424656ae305cc2ffa78ae.png)\n\nTwo angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘},$ a straight angle.\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, we have that $∠COB$ and $∠BOE$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm∠COB+m∠BOE={180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $∠BOE$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOE & ={180}^{∘}-m∠COB \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{47}^{∘} \\\\  & ={133}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
